{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>He and his brothers and all who went up with him.</b> On the return, Scripture places his brothers before the Egyptians who went up with him; but on the journey out, it placed the Egyptians before his brothers — as it says, ״וַיַּעֲלוּ אִתּוֹ כָּל עַבְדֵי פַרְעֹה״ and so on, and afterward ״כָּל בֵּית יוֹסֵף וְאֶחָיו.״ Rather, because they saw the honor that the kings of Canaan showed — they hung their crowns on Jacob's bier — they [the Egyptians] treated them with honor."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:26.591419913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}